    "80": [
      {
        "peer_id": 2033173701,
        "root_id": 41,
        "post_id": 80,
        "comments": [
          {
            "id": 44,
            "author": "Mrtko",
            "date": "2024-06-27T23:27:24+00:00",
            "body_html": "What are advantages compared to using a browser?",
            "reply_to": 41,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 47,
            "author": "Unknown author",
            "date": "2024-06-28T19:41:20+00:00",
            "body_html": "Offline\nFaster for slow computer - better for battery. Frontend is slow - here I feels like the native application.\nNo ads, trackers\nSome different functionalities, also with extensions for Thunderbird",
            "reply_to": 44,
            "has_media": false
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "81": [
      {
        "peer_id": 2033173701,
        "root_id": 42,
        "post_id": 81,
        "comments": [
          {
            "id": 43,
            "author": "Mrtko",
            "date": "2024-06-27T23:20:54+00:00",
            "body_html": "&gt; Sad that fanless laptops looks like unpopular\n\nWhy is it sad? I&#39;ve read they were released to marked just 3 months ago. People just don&#39;t want to buy a device with unpredictable behaviour",
            "reply_to": 42,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 45,
            "author": "Unknown author",
            "date": "2024-06-28T19:38:30+00:00",
            "body_html": "Why unpredictable - MacBook Air also fanless.",
            "reply_to": 43,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 46,
            "author": "Unknown author",
            "date": "2024-06-28T19:38:50+00:00",
            "body_html": "Already a lot of reviews",
            "reply_to": 43,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 48,
            "author": "Mrtko",
            "date": "2024-06-29T04:13:08+00:00",
            "body_html": "The reviews I read tell that some parts heat up above 100 degrees which can lead to slowing down the current processes, and in the long term to faster wear and tear.\n\nThe overheating may happen not only due to running multiple apps simultaneously, but also due to hot weather outside.\n\nSo, as long as there are laptops with fans, I will prefer them",
            "reply_to": 42,
            "has_media": false
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "82": [
      {
        "peer_id": 2033173701,
        "root_id": 49,
        "post_id": 82,
        "comments": [
          {
            "id": 50,
            "author": "Mrtko",
            "date": "2024-06-30T17:20:30+00:00",
            "body_html": "I think, one also could create their own site published on a free platform. Possible benefits include the following:\n\n- It may serve as a personal knowledge base. \n\n- It could help others.\n\n- You could share a link to reply to somebody&#39;s question (saves time).\n\n- You can use it as part of your portfolio to demonstrate your expertise and grow your personal brand.",
            "reply_to": 49,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 52,
            "author": "Unknown author",
            "date": "2024-07-01T05:37:17+00:00",
            "body_html": "Site will die after the death of the author - when nobody pay for hosting/domain.",
            "reply_to": 49,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 53,
            "author": "Unknown author",
            "date": "2024-07-01T05:38:45+00:00",
            "body_html": "External community is like independent validator - about views and rating (like Reddit, Habr).\n\nWiki will be improved by other people.",
            "reply_to": 49,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 54,
            "author": "Unknown author",
            "date": "2024-07-01T05:39:55+00:00",
            "body_html": "It is also possible to post to Linkedin - with ability to share and as a portfolio.",
            "reply_to": 49,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 55,
            "author": "Mrtko",
            "date": "2024-07-01T06:43:59+00:00",
            "body_html": "You&#39;re right. What do you think about GitHub/GitLab Pages for this purpose?",
            "reply_to": 49,
            "has_media": false
          },
          {
            "id": 657,
            "author": "Unknown author",
            "date": "2025-08-30T04:12:39+00:00",
            "body_html": "Maybe, better to contribute to something that already exists.",
            "reply_to": 49,
            "has_media": false
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
